course: dictionary
lesson: 6648
title: Nuisance: the thing that annoys you
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A nuisance is a person, animal or thing that annoys you or causes trouble. It is a noun, so you can have a nuisance or several nuisances. «I'm afraid it is the trouble you mind … I'm a nuisance, I know.» Toad says this about himself, so a nuisance can be someone who keeps getting in the way.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Flies, noise and rubbish are things that bother you without being dangerous. «The itch is a nuisance, not a sign of trouble.» So a nuisance can be annoying without being harmful. Ask yourself: does this thing bother me, even if it does not hurt me?
explain: Two phrases help too. "What a nuisance!" shows you are annoyed, and "make a nuisance of yourself" means bothering people on purpose. "Nuisance calls" are phone calls that keep interrupting you when you do not want them.
fact: A nuisance is a person, animal or thing that annoys you or causes trouble.
fact: «Ants are a nuisance but not dirty like cockroaches.» Ants annoy people, but they are not as dirty as cockroaches.
fact: Making a nuisance of yourself means bothering people.
fact: In law, a nuisance is something that unfairly disturbs your neighbours.
fact: «Friction can be a helper or a nuisance.» The same thing can be useful in one case and annoying in another.
exercise: «I'm afraid it is the trouble you mind … I'm a nuisance, I know.» What does nuisance mean here? | A pair of new shoes | *Someone who annoys people or gets in the way | A famous singer | A kind friend who always helps
exercise: Which of these is a nuisance? | *Flies buzzing around your lunch | A quiet park with a bench | A bright sunny morning | A warm blanket on a cold night
exercise: Find and copy the word that means something that annoys you. | helper | *nuisance | sentence | friction
test: "Making a nuisance of yourself" means what? | Hiding from everyone | Helping people with their homework | *Bothering people | Singing very quietly
test: «Ants are a nuisance but not dirty like cockroaches.» What does this tell you? | *Ants annoy us, but they are not as dirty as cockroaches | Ants are dirty and dangerous like cockroaches | Cockroaches are a nuisance, but ants are not | Ants are our best friends and never cause trouble
exam: What is a "nuisance call"? | A call to the fire brigade | A call that ends too early | A call from your best friend | *A phone call that keeps bothering you
